# LF everywhere -- in the index and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without `eol=lf`, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true rewrites text files
# to CRLF on checkout. That fights an editor configured for LF, and it makes
# `cargo fmt --check` depend on the machine it runs on rather than on the code.
# Setting it here rather than in local git config means CI and every clone get
# the same answer.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The ODF goldens are zip archives whose encrypted members the suite compares
# byte for byte. Git already auto-detects them as binary, but say so outright:
# a single CRLF substitution inside a compressed member would corrupt a fixture
# and surface as a decryption failure that reads like a crypto bug rather than
# a checkout artifact.
*.odt binary
